ng and let me know the results?\n\n1. Can you make regular calls and use mobile data (e.g., browse the web)?\n2. Are you seeing any error messages when trying to send an MMS?\n3. Is your phone connected to a 3G, 4G, or 5G network (not just 2G)?\n\nOnce you confirm, I’ll guide you through the next steps to resolve the MMS problem.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":10,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:05.542184","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":10,"usage":{"completion_tokens":148,"prompt_tokens":6926}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":11,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:06.665409","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_0LqKWw9lLQKfZW52Q5w41DpY","name":"check_status_bar","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":11,"usage":{"completion_tokens":12,"prompt_tokens":2553}},{"content":"Status Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📵 Data Disabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":12,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:06.665645","tool_call_id":"call_0LqKWw9lLQKfZW52Q5w41DpY","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":12,"usage":null},{"content":"Here’s what I see on my phone:\n\n- My signal is poor and it shows I’m connected to a 2G network.\n- Mobile data appears to be disabled.\n- I don’t see any specific error messages when trying to send an MMS, it just fails to send.\n\nWhat should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":13,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:08.000329","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":13,"usage":{"completion_tokens":65,"prompt_tokens":2593}},{"content":"Thank you for the details. MMS requires at least a 3G network and mobile data to be enabled. Here’s what you should do next:\n\n1. Enable mobile data on your phone.\n2. Change your network mode preference to allow 3G, 4G, or 5G (look for an option like “4G/5G preferred” or “Auto” in your network settings).\n\nAfter making these changes, try sending an MMS again. Let me know if you need step-by-step instructions for either of these actions or if you encounter any issues.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":14,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:09.639409","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":14,"usage":{"completion_tokens":118,"prompt_tokens":7143}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":15,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:11.291875","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_BAjuPwCoN6mWbzVcxp0MpOTQ","name":"toggle_data","requestor":"user_simulator"},{"arguments":{"mode":"4g_5g_preferred"},"id":"call_QoTrxL9vGrXZwInfhMiepKiH","name":"set_network_mode_preference","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":15,"usage":{"completion_tokens":51,"prompt_tokens":2780}},{"content":"Mobile Data is now ON.\nStatus Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":16,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:11.292365","tool_call_id":"call_BAjuPwCoN6mWbzVcxp0MpOTQ","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":16,"usage":null},{"content":"Preferred Network Mode set to: 4g_5g_preferred\nStatus Bar: 📶⁴ Excellent | 5G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":17,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:11.292459","tool_call_id":"call_QoTrxL9vGrXZwInfhMiepKiH","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":17,"usage":null},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":18,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:12.916731","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_BA7nYeFYwSmSqf80PC5Hyzs9","name":"can_send_mms","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":18,"usage":{"completion_tokens":13,"prompt_tokens":2895}},{"content":"Your messaging app cannot send MMS messages.","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":19,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:12.917172","tool_call_id":"call_BA7nYeFYwSmSqf80PC5Hyzs9","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":19,"usage":null},{"content":"I’ve enabled mobile data and changed my network mode to prefer 4G/5G. My phone now shows I’m connected to a 5G network with excellent signal, and data is enabled. However, I still can’t send MMS messages—there’s no error message, it just won’t send.\n\nWhat should I try next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":20,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:14.966630","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":20,"usage":{"completion_tokens":71,"prompt_tokens":2923}},{"content":"Thank you for updating your settings. Since you now have a strong 5G connection and mobile data is enabled, the next most common cause for MMS issues is incorrect APN (Access Point Name) settings, especially the MMSC URL.\n\nPlease check your APN settings on your phone and let me know if you see an MMSC URL listed. If you’re unsure how to check, I can guide you through resetting your APN settings to default, which often resolves MMS problems.\n\nWould you like instructions to reset your APN settings? After resetting, you’ll also need to reboot your device for the changes to take effect.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":21,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:16.701161","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":21,"usage":{"completion_tokens":128,"prompt_tokens":7336}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":22,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:17.635245","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_Nyg0rfG6VeepUePLc3LNbvdG","name":"check_apn_settings","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":22,"usage":{"completion_tokens":13,"prompt_tokens":3126}},{"content":"Current APN Name: internet\nMMSC URL (for picture messages): http://mms.carrier.com/mms/wapenc\n(These are technical settings, usually best left unchanged.)","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":23,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:17.635935","tool_call_id":"call_Nyg0rfG6VeepUePLc3LNbvdG","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":23,"usage":null},{"content":"I checked my APN settings, and the APN name is set to \"internet\" with the MMSC URL as \"http://mms.carrier.com/mms/wapenc.\" \n\nDo you still recommend resetting the APN settings and rebooting, or should I try something else first?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":24,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:18.850218","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":24,"usage":{"completion_tokens":62,"prompt_tokens":3185}},{"content":"Thank you for checking your APN settings. Since your APN name and MMSC URL appear to be set correctly, let’s try a couple of additional troubleshooting steps before resetting:\n\n1. Is Wi-Fi Calling enabled on your device? Sometimes, Wi-Fi Calling can interfere with MMS. If it is enabled, please turn it off and try sending an MMS again.\n2. Ensure your messaging app has permission to access storage and SMS. If you’re not sure, you can check your app permissions in your phone’s settings.\n\nIf you confirm both of these are set correctly and MMS still doesn’t work, then resetting your APN settings and rebooting your device would be the next best step.\n\nWould you like instructions for checking Wi-Fi Calling or app permissions, or are you ready to proceed with resetting the APN settings and rebooting?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":25,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:21.462615","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":25,"usage":{"completion_tokens":170,"prompt_tokens":7530}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":26,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:22.773675","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_A5D64Z6dUkxIAuDXaxS74i7n","name":"check_wifi_calling_status","requestor":"user_simulator"},{"arguments":{},"id":"call_3vlN3ZaXRVh86Wjx3aXrMElO","name":"check_installed_apps","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":26,"usage":{"completion_tokens":45,"prompt_tokens":3421}},{"content":"Wi-Fi Calling is currently turned OFF.","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":27,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:49:22.774119","tool_call_id":"call_A5D64Z6dUkxIAuDXaxS74i7n","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":27,"usage":null},{"content":"The following apps are installed on the phone: messaging, brows